# Forms and errors

User input goes through `to_form/2` and an Ecto changeset. Render field errors with `<.input>` (which uses public `<.error>`). Flash is for cross-cutting outcomes, not a substitute for field validation.

```elixir
# BAD
<.form for={%{}} as={:guest}>
  <.input name="display_name" value="" />
</.form>
# then put_flash(:error, "Name is required")

# GOOD
assign(socket, form: to_form(changeset, as: :song))
# template: <.form for={@form} id="queue-form"> <.input field={@form[:title]} />
```

LiveView uploads:

- Whitelist `accept` (never `:any`)
- Set `max_file_size`
- Show allowed types and size next to the input
- Handle `upload_errors/2` on `phx-change` — do not no-op validate handlers

Bound collections (per-room caps). Do not allow unbounded file append onto disk or object storage.
